WEBVTT

00:00:27.496 --> 00:00:31.121
Once you admit something is stolen,
aren’t you supposed to give it back?

00:00:31.121 --> 00:00:32.162
(Laughter)

00:00:32.204 --> 00:00:33.704
So if there’s anyone listening,

00:00:33.746 --> 00:00:37.204
who has a couple of hundred spare acres
that you’re feeling guilty about,

00:00:37.204 --> 00:00:39.246
just contact your local tribal government.

00:00:39.246 --> 00:00:41.537
We would be happy to relieve you
of that burden.

00:00:41.579 --> 00:00:42.704
(Laughter)

00:00:43.079 --> 00:00:44.871
That’s probably not you, right?

00:00:45.621 --> 00:00:49.037
Maybe you’ve heard of this movement
to return land to Indigenous people.

00:00:49.037 --> 00:00:51.496
But you're thinking,
"I can barely afford rent.

00:00:51.537 --> 00:00:53.996
What is it I'm supposed
to be giving back?"

00:00:54.871 --> 00:00:56.829
That's what I want to clarify today.

00:00:56.871 --> 00:01:01.954
Because not only is getting land back
in Indigenous hands in your best interests